1
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:34,547
我们一直在研究刚体运动群，即我们所确定的 R^n 刚体运动群——R^n 上保持两点间距离的运动群，有时也称为欧几里得运动群。
We've been studying the group of motions which we determine R^n—group of motions of R^n preserving the distance between two points, sometimes called the Euclidean motion group.

2
00:00:34,547 --> 00:00:52,079
上次我们证明了——虽然我们是对 n = 2 证明的，但如果你看证明，它是完全相同的——即如果你有一个 G 的有限子群 Gamma，
Last time we proved—well, we did this for n = 2, but if you look at the proof, it's exactly the same—that if you have a subgroup of G which is finite,

3
00:00:52,079 --> 00:01:25,080
那么 Gamma 必然固定某个点 P，即 R^n 中的某个点 P，因此它共轭于某个有限子群Gamma 落在 O 中，即固定原点 0 的子群 G_0。
then Gamma fixes a point P, some point P in R^n, so is conjugate to a finite subgroup Gamma inside of O, which is the subgroup G_0 fixing zero.

4
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:38,326
因此如果你寻找这个刚体运动群的有限子群，它们实际上全都由固定原点的子群的有限子群所决定。
So if you look for finite subgroups of this motion group, they're actually all determined by the finite subgroups of this subgroup fixing the origin.

5
00:01:38,326 --> 00:01:45,217
所以所固定的点就是这个重心或质心，正如在二维情形中一样。完全相同的论证在 n 维情形下同样成立。
So the point fixed is this barycenter or center of mass, exactly as it was in the two-dimensional case. The same argument works in the n-dimensional case.

6
00:01:45,217 --> 00:01:57,806
因此对其有限子群的分类便归结为对这里的有限子群的分类，这是一个很有趣的问题，且仅在极少数较小的 n 情形下被解决：n = 2、3 和 4。
So the classification of finite groups of this reduces to the classification of finite groups here, which is an interesting problem and has only been solved in very few small n cases: n = 2, 3, and 4.

7
00:01:57,806 --> 00:02:10,559
那么上次我们找出了二维正交群中的有限子群，我们发现它们分为两类。
So we did last time the finite subgroups in the orthogonal group of dimension two, and we found out that they were of two types.

8
00:02:10,559 --> 00:02:26,388
第一类是：我们令Gamma_+ 等于 Gamma 中行列式为 1 的元素 gamma，即 Gamma 中的旋转。
The first type was: we let Gamma_+ be equal to the gamma in Gamma whose determinant is 1, so the rotations in Gamma.

9
00:02:26,388 --> 00:02:42,680
第一类就是当 Gamma = Gamma_+ 时，此时 Gamma 是 n 阶循环群，由最小旋转角的旋转生成。
So the first type was when Gamma was equal to Gamma_+, and that was then Gamma was cyclic of order n, generated by the rotation of the smallest angle.

10
00:02:52,759 --> 00:03:00,270
第二类情形是 Gamma 包含指数为 2 的 Gamma_+。
And the second case was when Gamma contained Gamma_+ with index 2.

11
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:11,480
因此 Gamma 中存在行列式为 -1 的元素，而这些群是 2n 阶二面体群。
So there were elements in Gamma of determinant minus one, and those groups were dihedral of order 2n.

12
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:27,622
因此这一部分是 n 阶循环群，而非平凡陪集中的每个元素阶数都为 2 且都是反射，反射将该循环子群中的元素共轭变换为其逆元。
So that this was cyclic of order n, and everything in the non-trivial coset had order two and was a reflection, and the reflections conjugated elements in this cyclic subgroup to their inverses.

13
00:03:27,622 --> 00:03:46,920
所以我可以写出：若循环子群为 n 阶，且对所有属于 Gamma 减去Gamma_+ 的元素 r，有 r · Rot(theta) · r^{-1} = Rot(theta)^{-1} 且 r^2 = 1。
So I could write: if cyclic of order n, and that r · Rot(theta) · r^{-1} is equal to Rot(theta)^{-1} for all r in Gamma minus Gamma_+, r^2 is equal to 1.

14
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:56,568
现在如果你考虑正 n 边形，你就能得到这些群的一个很好的直观图景，因为正 n 边形在这些群的作用下保持不变。
Now you get a nice picture of these groups if you consider regular n-gons, because they're preserved by these groups.

15
00:03:56,568 --> 00:04:19,962
让我向大家展示一下这如何联系到——这些有限群如何联系到正 n 边形。我们可以想象从一个正 n 边形开始。让我看看能否画一个正八边形。也许这不太——不，这样画不行。
So let me show you how this relates to—how these finite groups relate to regular n-gons. So one imagines starting a regular n-gon. Let me see if I can draw a a regular octagon. Maybe this isn't—no, that's not going to work.

16
00:04:19,962 --> 00:04:28,680
我在画什么呢？我们来画一个正六边形吧。为什么不画正六边形呢？我觉得那个我应该能画出来。
What am I drawing here? Let's draw a regular hexagon. Why don't we do a regular hexagon? That I think I may be able to do.

17
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,999
这对应于 n = 6 的情形。
This would be the case n = 6.

18
00:04:36,999 --> 00:04:48,772
如果你考虑 6 阶循环群的作用，它把这个点映到那个点，因为这是一个旋转 60° 的变换，这就是 6 阶旋转。
So if you think of the action of the cyclic group of order six, it takes this point to that point, because this is a rotation through 60°, that's the rotation of order 6.

19
00:04:48,772 --> 00:05:01,588
theta 是尽可能小的角，所以 theta = 2pi/n，因为只有这样的旋转在执行 n 次后才会把你带回到恒等变换。所以它会把这个顶点映到这个顶点。
theta is as small as possible, so theta would be 2pi/n, because that would be the rotation that if you did it n times would take you back to the identity. So it would take this point to this point.

20
00:05:01,588 --> 00:05:08,520
它会把这个点映到这个点。因此群的一个轨道就是这个正六边形的全体顶点。
It would take this point to this point. So one orbit of the group would be the vertices of this regular hexagon.

21
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:12,893
但你也可以让 12 阶二面体群作用在这个六边形上。
But you could also have the dihedral group of order 12 acting on that hexagon.

22
00:05:12,893 --> 00:05:30,396
因为如果你还考虑关于直线的反射——那些穿过对边中点的直线，有三条这样的直线穿过对边中点。这就给出了三个保持正六边形不变的反射。
Because if you also thought about reflection through the lines that go between the midpoints of the edges, there are three such lines that go through the midpoints of the edges. That gives you three reflections that preserve the regular hexagon.

23
00:05:30,396 --> 00:05:33,719
此外你还有连接对顶点的直线。
And you also have the lines that connect the vertices.

24
00:05:33,719 --> 00:05:41,130
还有另外三条这样的直线。这就给出了六条直线，关于它们作反射可以保持正六边形不变。
There are three more lines like that. So that gives you six lines through which you can take the reflection and preserve this regular hexagon.

25
00:05:41,130 --> 00:05:52,831
而这些正是12 阶二面体群中不在 6 阶循环群里的六个元素。现在注意，这些反射具有两种不同的类型。
And those are the six elements in the dihedral group of order 12 that are not in the cyclic group of order six. Now notice they come in two different flavors, those type of reflections.

26
00:05:52,831 --> 00:06:04,114
有三条是连接对顶点的，另外三条则是对边的垂直平分线。
There are the three ones that connect pairs of opposite vertices, and then there are the three that are through the perpendiculars of the opposite sides.

27
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:25,240
因此 12 阶二面体群中的这六个反射实际上被分为 3 + 3，其中一组是穿过顶点的线，另一组是穿过边中点的线。
So the six reflections in the dihedral group of order 12 really are grouped as three + three, where these are lines through vertices and these are lines through the sides.

28
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,295
这是六边形的情形。
Whereas that happens for the hexagon.

29
00:06:28,295 --> 00:06:49,256
而如果我们取三角形，对应于 6 阶二面体群的情形，这对应于 n = 3，即 6 阶二面体群，正如我说过的，它同构于三个字母上的对称群 S_3。
If instead we took the triangle, which would be the case of the dihedral group of order six, this would be, you know, n = 3, dihedral group of order six, which I said was the same thing as the symmetric group on three letters.

30
00:06:49,256 --> 00:06:59,237
关于其作反射以保持该三角形不变的直线，都是穿过一个顶点和其对边的。
The lines through which you can reflect to preserve this triangle go through a vertex and the opposite side.

31
00:06:59,237 --> 00:07:06,800
所以——好吧，我画得不太出色，但确实有三条直线关于其反射能保持三角形不变，它们是其中的三个对合元——
So there—well, I didn't draw that too brilliantly, but there are three lines through which you can reflect and preserve this triangle,

32
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:26,039
在此时 Gamma 减去 Gamma_+ 中有三个元素，它们是三个字母上的对称群中阶数为 2 的三个元素，且它们全都是同一种类型：穿过一个顶点和一条对边。
and those are the three involutions in—there are three elements in Gamma minus Gamma_+ in this case, those are the three elements of order two in the symmetric group on three letters, and they're all of the same type: one vertex, one side.

33
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:36,810
此时发生的情况是，Gamma 减去 Gamma_+ 中的这三个元素全都互相共轭，因为它们在几何上是全等的。
And what happens is that in this case the three elements in Gamma minus Gamma_+ are all conjugate, because they're all geometrically similar.

34
00:07:36,810 --> 00:07:48,738
而在前一种情形中，Gamma 减去 Gamma_+ 中的六个元素构成了两个共轭类：这种类型的三条，以及另一种类型的三条。
Whereas in this case the six elements in Gamma minus Gamma_+ form two conjugacy classes: the three of this type and then the three of this type.

35
00:07:48,738 --> 00:07:53,582
这是区分偶数阶和奇数阶二面体群的普遍现象。
And that's a general phenomenon that distinguishes even and odd dihedral groups.

36
00:07:53,582 --> 00:08:07,160
当 n 为奇数时——我们还会回过头讲这个——在Gamma 减去 Gamma_+ 中的元素在 Gamma 中全部互相共轭。
When n is odd—we're going to get back to this—the elements in Gamma minus Gamma_+ are all conjugate in Gamma.

37
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:21,395
当 n 为偶数时，元素构成两个共轭类，因为你有两种不同类型的可以关于其反射并保持图形不变的直线：穿过边的线和穿过顶点的线。
When n is even, in this case the elements form two conjugacy classes because you have two different types of lines through which you can reflect and preserve the figure: the ones through the edges and the ones through the vertices.

38
00:08:21,395 --> 00:08:33,135
而在奇数情形下，每条这样的直线都同时穿过一条边和一个顶点。因此我们稍后会回到二面体群中的共轭性，但这种几何图景有助于大家区分偶数和奇数的情形。
Whereas in the odd case each such line goes through an edge and a vertex. So we'll come back to conjugacy in the dihedral group, but that geometric picture helps you distinguish the even and odd cases.

39
00:08:33,135 --> 00:08:42,538
顺便说一句，还有另一个我们之前见过的二面体群：6 阶二面体群是三个字母上的对称群；4 阶二面体群就是克莱因四元群，因为如果你想一想 4 阶二面体群，正n 边形其实就是一个二边形（2-gon）。
By the way, there's one other dihedral group that we've seen before: the dihedral group of order six is the symmetric group on three letters.

40
00:08:51,747 --> 00:08:57,571
这有点搞笑，n = 2。它只有两条边，叠在一起，并没有真正分开。
It's kind of stupid, n = 2. It only has two sides. They're right on top of each other. They didn't really separate.

41
00:08:57,571 --> 00:09:00,680
它们试图长成这样：上面一条、下面一条，但没有足够的空间。
They're trying to look like this: one up here and one down there, but they didn't have enough room.

42
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:04,199
而反射就是这个反射。
And the reflection is this reflection.

43
00:09:04,199 --> 00:09:10,746
那就是非平凡陪集中的元素，而旋转则是旋转 180 度。
That's the element in the non-trivial coset, whereas the rotation is the rotation by 180 degrees.

44
00:09:10,746 --> 00:09:21,655
如果你考虑它们的乘积，如果你考虑由这两个对合元生成的群，它们彼此交换。这就是克莱因四元群。它包含三个对合元以及单位元。
And if you think of the product, if you think of the group generated by those two involutions, they commute with each other. And that's the Klein 4-group. It has three involutions in it and the identity element.

45
00:09:21,655 --> 00:09:33,880
而所有其他的二面体群 D_{2n}（n >= 3）都是非交换的，并且作用在正 n 边形上。
Whereas all the other dihedral groups D_{2n}, n >= 3, are non-abelian and act on the regular n-gon.

46
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:45,326
对。所以，D_4 是二边形，而不是四边形？D_{2n} 作用在正 n 边形上。
Yeah. So, so D_4 is the 2-gon, not the 4-gon? The D_{2n} acts on the regular n-gon.

47
00:09:45,326 --> 00:09:47,079
所以，D_4 是二边形，而不是四边形？D_{2n} 作用在正 n 边形上。
So, so D_4 is the 2-gon, not the 4-gon? The D_{2n} acts on the regular n-gon.

48
