But in the finite group case, we didn't really need this whole group of motions.

63
00:11:39,079 --> 00:11:43,862
我们本可以直接考察正交群的有限子群，因为它们都固定某一个点。
We could have just asked for the finite groups of the orthogonal group, because they preserve some point.

64
00:11:43,862 --> 00:11:50,120
但今天我们要进入真正有趣的主题，它比有限群更为一般。
But today we're going to get into the really interesting subject which is more general than finite groups.

65
00:11:50,120 --> 00:12:20,360
更一般地，我们希望对G 中的离散子群 Gamma 进行分类——我马上会解释离散的含义。离散子群的意思如下。记住 G 中的元素都是平移和旋转的乘积。
More generally, we want to classify the discrete—and I'm going to say what that means—subgroups Gamma in G. So a discrete subgroup means the following. Remember that elements in G are products of translations and rotations.

66
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:39,791
所以这里的一切、G 中的任何元素都唯一地表示为一个向量平移乘以——好吧，至少抱歉，乘以一个O 中的元素，而该元素可写为向量平移、按角度旋转。
So everything here, any element in G, is uniquely expressed as the product of a translation by a vector times the—well, at least, sorry, times an element in O, and that element can be written as either translation by a vector, rotation by an angle.

67
00:12:39,791 --> 00:12:54,000
抱歉口误，好的，离散子群：我来告诉大家在 G = R^2 ⋊ O(2) 中的离散子群是什么。
Well, sorry, we're just going to go: all right, discrete subgroups: I'll tell you what a discrete subgroup is in G, which is R^2 ⋊ O(2).

68
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:19,051
离散意味着 Gamma 不包含任意小的旋转或平移。
Discrete means that Gamma does not contain arbitrarily small rotations or translations.

69
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:31,799
我必须说明这是什么意思：所谓任意小，是指如果它包含一个向量平移，那么该向量的大小是有下界的；如果它包含旋转，那么该旋转的角度也是有正下界的，
So I have to say what that means, and arbitrarily small means that if it contains a translation by a vector, the size of that vector is bounded from below; and if it contains a rotation,

70
00:13:31,799 --> 00:13:55,626
与 Gamma 中的元素无关；也就是说，存在一个epsilon > 0，使得若 t_b 在 Gamma 中，则向量 b 的范数 ||b|| >= epsilon；
the angle of that rotation is bounded from below, independent of what elements in Gamma; i.e., there is an epsilon > 0, so that if t_b is in Gamma, the size of b as a vector is larger than or equal to epsilon;

71
00:13:55,626 --> 00:14:10,439
若旋转角为 theta 的旋转在Gamma 中，则 |theta| >= epsilon。你不能平移任意小的元素，也不能旋转任意小的元素。
and if rotation by theta is in Gamma, the size of theta is bigger than or equal to epsilon. You can't translate by arbitrarily small elements. You can't rotate by arbitrarily small elements.

72
00:14:10,439 --> 00:14:21,468
这是因为我们基本上清楚这里的元素长什么样。这里的子群是离散的究竟意味着什么？我们在 O 中有关于什么是小元素的概念。
That's because we know basically what things in here look like. What does it mean for something in here to be discrete? Well, we have a notion of what a small element is in O.

73
00:14:21,468 --> 00:14:29,327
即这些群 O(n) 上面有距离的概念。因此一个任意元素看起来就像这样。
Namely, these groups have a notion of distance on them, O(n). So, an arbitrary element looks like this.

74
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:57,472
我们也可以要求 Gamma 不包含任意小的平移，即 ||b|| >= epsilon，并且 A 不会任意接近单位元，含义是矩阵 A 的元素与单位矩阵的对应元素之差不全落在 epsilon 之内。
We could also ask that Gamma not contain arbitrarily small translations, so ||b|| >= epsilon, and A is not arbitrarily close to the identity element, in the sense that the matrix entries of A are not all within epsilon of the matrix entries of the identity element.

75
00:14:57,472 --> 00:15:02,480
这是一种将“旋转角至少有一个正下界”加以推广的方式。
That's a way of generalizing this rotation is at least a large angle.

76
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:13,793
我的意思是，这个特殊的变换——记住它是[[cos theta, -sin theta], [sin theta, cos theta]]——
By that I'm saying that this particular transformation, which remember is [cos theta, -sin theta; sin theta, cos theta]—to say that theta is greater

77
00:15:13,793 --> 00:15:29,353
说 |theta| >= epsilon 就是说该矩阵不会任意接近单位矩阵，因为如果 theta 变得过小，sin(theta) 就会极其接近 0，而 cos(theta) 就会极其接近1。
than or equal to epsilon says that this matrix is not arbitrarily close to the identity element, because if theta got too small, the sin(theta) would get very close to 0 and cos(theta) would become very close to 1.

78
00:15:29,353 --> 00:15:43,982
因此一般而言，我们可以要求 Gamma 的元素不能离恒等变换过近；我们在实矩阵上有范数或大小的概念，在实向量上也有大小的概念，这使我们能够给出这个陈述。
So in general we can ask that the elements of Gamma not be too close to the identity transformation, and the fact that we have a notion of size on real matrices and we have a notion of size on real vectors allows us to make that statement.

79
00:15:43,982 --> 00:15:58,104
有限群自然具备这种性质，因为有限群只有有限个元素。你只需找出所涉及的最小旋转角、最小平移距离，那就是你的 epsilon。
Now finite groups have that property, because finite groups are only a finite number of elements in the group. So you just find what is the smallest angle of rotation involved, what is the smallest distance of translation involved, and that's your epsilon.

80
00:15:58,104 --> 00:15:59,594
但事实是，这种性质在无限群中也可以存在。
But the fact is this can exist for infinite groups too.

81
00:15:59,594 --> 00:16:24,846
所以我来给大家举一个无限离散子群（且不是有限群）的简单例子：一个落在 G 中的无限离散子群 Gamma，即 R^n ⋊ O(n)。
So I'll give you a simple example of an infinite discrete subgroup that isn't finite: an infinite discrete Gamma inside of G, R^n ⋊ O(n).

82
00:16:24,846 --> 00:16:58,706
设 b 是一个非零向量。令 Gamma 为由平移 t_b 生成的循环群。平移变换具有无限阶。如果你从原点出发，这里是向量 b，它把原点映到 b。如果你再执行一次，你就到了 2b。
Let b be a non-zero vector. Take Gamma equal to the cyclic group generated by translations in b. So translations have infinite order. If you start at the origin and here's the vector b, it takes your origin up to b. And then if you do it again, you'd go to 2b.

83
00:16:58,706 --> 00:17:04,344
然后再做一次就得到 3b，你永远回不到原点，因为你越走越远。
And then if you take it again, you get a 3b, and you never get back to the origin because you keep moving further away.

84
00:17:04,344 --> 00:17:09,215
同时你还有反向的平移映到 -b、-2b 等等。
And you also have the translations backwards to -b and to -2b, etc.

85
00:17:09,215 --> 00:17:26,680
所以这是非常好的一个无限离散群的例子，因为它不包含任意小的平移，因为其中没有任何平移的平移距离小于 ||b||。
So that's a perfectly good example of an infinite discrete group, because it doesn't contain arbitrarily small translations, because no translation has distance less than ||b|| in it.

86
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:40,583
现在我们要做的是对这个群的所有可能离散子群进行分类；其中当然包含有限群，但同时也有包含无限阶元素的群，我们也想找出那些群。
Now what we're going to do is classify all possible discrete groups of this group, and that—of course we have the finite groups, but then we have the groups that have elements of infinite order in them, and we want to find those groups too.

87
00:17:40,583 --> 00:17:47,080
这是一个极其美妙的问题，正如教材所描述的，它与各种壁纸图案的设计息息相关。
That's a beautiful problem that's related to, as the book describes various designs of wallpaper.

88
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:56,280
它给出了你在平面上能够设计的、具有对称图案的所有不同类型的壁纸。
So it gives you all the different types of wallpaper you can design on the plane that have symmetric patterns.

89
00:17:56,280 --> 00:18:02,599
好。那么我们的方法大致是这样的。
Okay. So the method goes something like this.

90
00:18:02,599 --> 00:18:15,880
第一步：设 Gamma 是 G 的一个离散子群，我们将考虑两样东西。
The first step: let Gamma be a discrete subgroup of G, and we're going to consider two things.

91
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:24,760
首先，我们要考虑 L，即 Gamma 与平移子群的交集。
First, we're going to consider L, which is the intersection of Gamma with the subgroup of translations.

92
00:18:28,839 --> 00:18:39,328
它是 Gamma 的一个子群，因为 Gamma 是群。这被称为格点群（lattice）或 Gamma 的加法子群。
That's a subgroup of Gamma because Gamma is a group. And this is called the lattice or the additive subgroup of Gamma.

93
00:18:39,328 --> 00:18:54,694
然后我们要考虑的第二样东西是 Gamma 在 O(2) 中的像 Gamma-bar，它落在我们将 G 模去正规子群 R^2 所得到的商群中。
And then the second thing we're going to consider is the image Gamma-bar of Gamma in O(2), in the quotient which we view as G modulo the normal subgroup R^2.

94
00:18:54,694 --> 00:19:00,760
所以这不是看作子群，而是在商群之中。
So this is not viewed as a subgroup; this is in the quotient group.

95
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:15,104
那个同态会把 L 映到平凡元，对吧？该同态的核正是 Gamma 与平移子群的交集。所以这正好是 Gamma 模去其正规子群 L。
Now that homomorphism will kill L, right? The kernel of that homomorphism is the intersection of Gamma with translations. So this is just Gamma modulo its normal subgroup L.

96
00:19:15,104 --> 00:19:19,585
由这两个部分，我们就可以组装出我们的离散群 Gamma。
And out of those two pieces, we're going to assemble our discrete group Gamma.

97
00:19:19,585 --> 00:19:36,040
至于有限群——如果我们有一个有限群，那么该有限群就等于它在 O(2) 中的像，而我们之前已经完成了分类，因为我们知道了 O(2) 的所有有限子群，有限群根本不包含任何非平凡平移。
Now our finite groups—if we had a finite group, then the finite group would be equal to its image in O(2), and we would have classified it, because we know all the finite subgroups of O(2), because finite groups contain no translations at all.

98
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:44,054
因此这个定理的新部分将针对 L 是非平凡的情形，即对应于那边的例子。
So the new part of this theorem will be for groups where L is non-trivial, i.e., for this one over there.

99
00:19:44,054 --> 00:19:55,479
这里的例子中，L——在这里它正好等于 L，而 Gamma-bar 等于平凡群 {1}，因为所有元素都在映到O(2) 的映射的核中。
That one here, L— so here this would be equal to L and Gamma-bar would be equal to {1}, because everything would be in the kernel of the map to O(2).

100
00:19:55,479 --> 00:20:06,040
所以这有时被称为离散群的加法部分，而另一个则是它在 O(2) 中的像或点群（点稳定子）。
So this is sometimes called the additive part of the discrete group, and this would be the image of it, or the point stabilizer of it in O(2).

101
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:15,479
好。所以我给出第一个定理：我们先弄清楚 L 可以长成什么样，然后再弄清楚 Gamma-bar 可以长成什么样。
Okay. So I claim the first theorem: let's first figure out what L can look like, and then we'll figure out what Gamma-bar can look like.

102
00:20:15,479 --> 00:20:29,800
第一步：对于 L 而言，有哪些可能性？
First step: what are the possibilities for L?

103
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:35,000
我断言 L 只有三种可能性，仅此而已。
So I claim there are three possibilities for L, and that's it.

104
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:41,479
好，第一种是 L = {0}。
Okay, one is that L can be {0}.

105
00:20:41,479 --> 00:20:46,039
那就是 Gamma 为有限群的情形。
That's the case when Gamma is finite.

106
00:20:51,400 --> 00:21:14,852
第二种：即我们这里的例子，L 可以是某个固定向量的所有整数倍，其中 b 是 R^2 中的非零向量——某个固定向量的所有平移；这当然具备不包含任意小平移的性质。
Two: the case we had here, L can be all integer multiples of a fixed vector, where b is non-zero in R^2—all translates of a fixed vector; that certainly has the property that it doesn't contain arbitrarily small translations.

107
00:21:14,852 --> 00:21:39,800
第三种可能性是：L 可以是一个向量的所有整数倍加上另一个向量的所有整数倍，其中 a 和 b 在 R^2 中线性无关，也就是 a 与 b 构成了 R^2 的一组基。
And the third possibility is that L can be all integer multiples of one vector plus all integer multiples of another vector, where a and b are linearly independent over R in R^2, namely where a and b give a basis.

108
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:47,880
所以对于这个点阵群只有这三种可能。顺便说一句，第三种情形通常被严格称为“格”（lattice）。
So there are only three possibilities for this lattice group. By the way, this case is usually called a lattice.

109
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:55,719
它是关于 a 和 b 的平移所生成的群，其中 a 和 b 是线性无关的向量。
So it's a group generated by translations in a and b, where a and b are linearly independent vectors.

110
00:21:55,719 --> 00:22:02,120
好。现在我要向大家证明，L 就只有这三种可能性。
Okay. Now I'm going to show you that those are the only three possibilities for L.

111
00:22:03,719 --> 00:22:26,106
所以我断言：在证明之前，我们先做几点初步观察。如果你有两个属于 L 的向量，那么 b - b' 属于 L，作为 R^2 中的向量。
So I claim: let's make a couple of initial observations before we prove this. If you have two vectors in L, then b - b' is in L as a vector in R^2.

112
00:22:26,106 --> 00:22:38,359
因此对于某个固定的 epsilon，范数 ||b - b'|| >= epsilon。
So the norm of b - b' is bigger than epsilon for some fixed epsilon.

113
00:22:38,359 --> 00:22:44,160
这是因为这意味着你有按 b 的平移，也有按 b' 的平移。
Well, that's because this says you have translation by b, you have translation by b'.

114
00:22:44,160 --> 00:23:04,829
这之所以成立是因为按 t_b · (t_{b'})^{-1} 平移的向量就是 t_{b - b'}。
So this comes up because this would be the vector of translation by t_b · (t_{b'})^{-1}, which is t_{b - b'}.

115
00:23:04,829 --> 00:23:12,187
而根据我们的假设，Gamma 中的所有非零平移的大小至少为 epsilon，其范数至少为 epsilon。
And all translations by our hypothesis in Gamma have size at least epsilon, the norm of which is at least epsilon.

116
00:23:12,187 --> 00:23:22,359
换句话说，如果你在这个 R^2 的子集中有两个向量，它们彼此之间不能太靠近。向量之间不能任意接近：这是最根本的观察。
So in other words, if you have two vectors in this subset of R^2, they can't be too close to each other. Vectors can't get too close to each other: that's the essential observation.

117
00:23:22,359 --> 00:23:31,994
好的。现在，这一条件很清楚。我们当然可能有 L = {0}。
Okay. Now, so this condition is clear. We could certainly have L = {0}.

118
00:23:31,994 --> 00:24:01,640
因此假设 L != {0}，那么就有两种可能性。第二种情形——第一种很显然，你当然可以有 L = {0}——L != {0} 的情形中，首先是所有L 中的向量都落在同一条直线上。
So assume L is not equal to {0}, and so there are two possibilities. Case two—so one is clear, you can certainly have L = {0} too—L is not equal to {0} is the case where all vectors in L lie on a line.

119
00:24:08,093 --> 00:24:16,839
它们要么全在一条直线上，要么不在；{0} 是最简单的情形，此时它们张成一个零维空间；在这里，它们全都是落在某条直线上的向量。
Either they lie on a line or they don't; {0} is the simplest case where they span a zero-dimensional space; here they would all be vectors somewhere on a line.

120
00:24:16,839 --> 00:24:25,241
好，现在我们令 b 为该直线上最接近原点的非零向量。
Okay, now we let b be the vector on that line which is closest to the origin.

121
00:24:25,241 --> 00:24:40,759
顺便说一句，这并不是唯一的，但必定存在这样的向量，因为我们不可能有向量任意接近原点。
And now that's not unique, by the way, but there has to be such a vector, because we don't get vectors arbitrarily close to the origin.

122
00:24:40,759 --> 00:24:50,900
必定存在一个最靠近原点的向量；因为如果找不到最近的，我就能找到一列越来越接近原点的向量。
There must be one that's closest, because if I couldn't find one that was closest, I could find a sequence of vectors getting closer and closer and closer to the origin.

123
00:24:50,900 --> 00:24:56,990
但是原点显然在 L 中，且非零向量必须与原点保持一个有下界的距离。因此必定存在一个最近的向量。
But the origin is certainly in L, and vectors have to stay a bounded distance away from the origin. So there must be one that's closest.

124
00:24:56,990 --> 00:25:05,437
现在我说：取 b 为最近的那个。当然这并不是唯一的，因为一旦我找到了 b，我也可以找到 -b，它具有相同的距离。
Now I'm saying: take b to be the closest one. But of course that's not unique, because once I found b, I could have also found -b, which is the same distance.

125
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:08,484
但只需任取一个最接近原点的向量即可。
But just use one that's closest to the origin.

126
00:25:08,484 --> 00:25:19,415
那么我断言 L 中的所有向量都只是b 的整数倍。也就是说我们在情形 2 中。
Then I claim that all vectors in L are just multiples of b. Namely, I'm in Case 2.

127
00:25:19,415 --> 00:25:25,719
所以情形 1 是当 L 只有零向量时出现的；而情形 2 是当所有向量都在一条直线上时得到的。
So this case arises if there's nothing in L; this case is what you get if everything is on a line.

128
00:25:25,719 --> 00:25:30,040
好的，为什么呢？这就是我们著名的欧几里得辗转相除法论证。
Okay, why is that? Well, this is our famous Euclidean algorithm argument.

129
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:46,720
假设我在 L 中还有别的向量：这里是我的 b'。我把 b' 写成 b 的某个整数倍加上余项 r_0 · b：b' = n · b + r_0 · b，其中 n 是整数，
Suppose I had something else on L: here's my b'. And I write b' as some multiple of b plus a remainder r_0 · b, where n is an integer and r_0 is some

130
00:25:46,720 --> 00:26:01,230
r_0 满足 0 <= r_0 < 1，因为我只要沿着 b 的倍数一步步向前走，直到正好走到 b' 之前的一个，然后再走一步就超过了b'。
number between 0 and 1, because I just keep marching out by multiples of b until I get one right before b', and then I have one after b'.

131
00:26:01,230 --> 00:26:06,520
所以 b' 就是比如 2 · b 加上 b 的介于 0 到 1 之间的某个倍数。
So b' would be some 2 · b plus some multiple of b between 0 and 1.

132
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:35,319
现在如果 r_0 不等于 0，那么 r_0 · b 属于 L，因为 b' 在 L 中，且 n · b 也在 L 中，并且它会比 b 更短，对吧，因为 r_0 < 1。因此，r_0 必须等于 0，这说明格中的一切都是 b 的整数倍。
Now if r_0 is not equal to 0, then r_0 · b is in L, because this is in L and this is in L, and it would be shorter than b, right, because r_0 is of length less than 1. Consequently, r_0 has to be equal to zero, which says that everything in the lattice is a multiple of b.

133
00:26:35,319 --> 00:26:39,000
也就是说，点阵就是 b 的全体整数倍 Z · b。
Namely, the lattice is just integer multiples of b.

134
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:45,320
我们已经在循环群中多次见到这种欧几里得辗转相除法论证了。
So we've seen that Euclidean algorithm argument a couple of times for cyclic groups.

135
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:53,400
现在有趣的部分来了：现在假设它们不全在同一条直线上。
Now comes the fun part: now suppose that they're not all on a line.

136
00:26:57,160 --> 00:27:00,720
这就是情形 3。
This is Case 3.

137
00:27:05,959 --> 00:27:25,754
换句话说，L 包含 R^2 的一组基。L 中必定有两个不共线的向量，因此存在一组基。
In other words, L contains a basis of R^2. There have to be two vectors in L, not both on the same line, so there is a basis.

138
00:27:26,147 --> 00:27:45,595
好的。现在取这组基，不妨设为 a 和 b。我们要合理地组织步骤。我们做的第一件事是取 b 所张成的直线，并且让 b 为最短向量。
Okay. Now take the basis, say a and b. So we want to organize ourselves correctly. The first thing we do is we take the line spanned by b, and we let b be the shortest vector.

139
00:27:45,595 --> 00:27:56,348
我们不妨要求这是 L 在直线 R · b 上的最短非零向量。
We might as well insist that this is the shortest vector in L on the line R · b.

140
00:27:56,348 --> 00:28:11,841
如果原本不是，为什么不把它换成同一直线上落在 L 中的另一个最短向量呢？同样，我们不妨假设 a 是L 在直线 R · a 上的最短向量。
Why not replace it by another vector on the same line which is in L if it isn't? And we might as well assume this is the shortest in L on the line R · a.

141
00:28:11,841 --> 00:28:23,119
它们仍然线性无关。我们有 b 张成的线，有 a 张成的线，我们在每条线上都取最短的向量。
They're still linearly independent. We had the line spanned by b, we had the line spanned by a, and we just go to the shortest vector on each such line.

142
00:28:23,119 --> 00:28:27,160
我们要看看这是否能给出我想要的生成元。
And we're going to see if that gives us our generators that I want.

143
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:55,559
好的。在进一步讨论之前，我想先证明一个小引理：如果 S 是 R^2 的一个有界子集，那么 S 与这个子群 L 的交集是有限集。
All right. Now before I go any further, I want to prove a little lemma that says if S is a bounded subset of R^2, then the intersection of S with this subgroup L is finite.

144
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:19,902
如果不是有限集——这只是回到大家的微积分或拓扑学课程：这是我们的有界集。任何有界集都可以放进一个大球内。因此只需证明任何大球与 L 的交集是有限的。
Well, if it were—this is just back to your course in calculus or topology: here's our bounded set. Any bounded set could be put inside of a large ball. So it's enough to show that any large ball which intersects L is finite.

145
00:29:19,902 --> 00:29:32,692
如果它是无限的，你在一个有界集里就有无限多个元素。有界集中的无限点集必然拥有一个收敛子列，对吧？这就是我们在紧致性中证明的定理。
Well, if it were infinite, you have an infinite number of elements in a bounded set. An infinite number of elements in a bounded set has a convergent subsequence, right? That's what we prove about compactness.

146
00:29:32,692 --> 00:29:48,400
所以设想我们在 L 中有一列点收敛到这个极限点，将其中两项相减，你就会得到 L 中一列收敛到原点的元素，因为你总可以作平移相减，
So imagine that we have a convergent sequence of elements in L to this point, and subtract one of those elements, and you'd get a sequence of elements in L converging to the origin, because you can always translate by something there,

147
00:29:48,400 --> 00:30:05,200
于是你就会得到L 中任意小的非零元素，而这是不允许的；换句话说，我们也证明了 L 中任意两点间的距离始终大于等于 epsilon。所以你不可能有收敛子列。
and then you'd get arbitrarily small elements in L, which you're not allowed to do; or in other words, we also showed that the distances remain greater than or equal to epsilon for any two elements in L. So you couldn't have a convergent subsequence.

148
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:45,719
证明：若无限，可选出收敛子列；但这是不可能的，因为 L 中的任何点列都不可能是柯西序列，对吧？因为不同元素间的距离无法任意接近。所以这是群论与拓扑学的一个有趣结合。
Proof: if infinite, can choose a convergent subsequence, but this is impossible, as no sequence of elements in L is Cauchy, right? Because the distances between elements can't get arbitrarily close. So this is an interesting combination of group theory and topology.

149
00:30:45,719 --> 00:30:48,917
所以我们要牢记这个引理。
So we're going to bear this lemma in mind.

150
00:30:48,917 --> 00:31:11,320
现在考虑——我们仍在这里研究情形 3——考虑由 a 和 b 张成的平行四边形。这里是向量 a + b。
Now consider—we're still working on Case 3 here— consider the parallelogram spanned by a and b. Here's the vector, I guess, a + b.

151
00:31:12,839 --> 00:31:23,959
设该平行四边形为 P。我们选取了 a 为其所在线上的最短向量，b 为其所在线上的最短向量，然后取它们所张成的平行四边形。
Let's call that parallelogram P. So we chose a the shortest vector on its line, b the shortest vector on its line, and then we take the parallelogram that they span.

152
00:31:23,959 --> 00:31:26,440
这里是原点 0。
Here's 0.

153
00:31:26,440 --> 00:32:10,504
好的。现在的问题是：在——看看我设定得对不对，我想是对的——嗯，啊，好的：更换这个平行四边形。在该平行四边形内部，可能存在某个向量比点 b 更靠近这条直线。
Okay. Now the question is: are there any points in L on—let's see if I set this up right, I think I have it right. Um, ah, okay: replace this parallelogram. There might be some vector inside the parallelogram that is closer to this line than the point b.

154
00:32:10,504 --> 00:32:21,531
也就是说，点 b 到从 0 到 a 的直线有一个距离。而在该平行四边形与 L 的交集中，可能有某个点比 b 更靠近这条直线。
Namely, there's some distance that b has from the line 0 to a. And there might be some point in the parallelogram intersect L that's closer to this line than b.

155
00:32:21,531 --> 00:32:36,608
所以可能存在这里的一个点 b' 或类似的点，它比 b 更接近该直线。好的，在该平行四边形内部，L 的点只有有限多个，因为该平行四边形是一个有界集。
So maybe there's a point here, b' or something of that nature, which is closer to this line than b. Okay, there are only finitely many points of L inside of this parallelogram because this parallelogram is a bounded set.

156
00:32:36,608 --> 00:32:38,675
所以 L 中只可能有有限多个点。
So there are only finitely many possible points in L.

157
00:32:38,675 --> 00:32:53,430
于是我们考察该平行四边形内属于 L 的所有点，看是否有任何点比点 b 更靠近这条直线；如果我们找到了几个，我们现在就用最近的那个点来替换 b。
So we look at all the points in L inside of this parallelogram and we see if there are any of them that are closer to this line than the point b is, and we find a few, and we replace b now by the closest point.

158
00:32:53,430 --> 00:33:16,056
也就是说，用 P ∩ L 中最靠近a 张成的直线（但不落在其上）的点来替换 L 中的 b。
So replace b in L by the point in P ∩ L closest to the line spanned by a, but not on it.

159
00:33:16,056 --> 00:33:17,932
也许没有任何点比 b 更近。
Maybe there are no points that are closer than b.

160
00:33:17,932 --> 00:33:29,709
但如果 P 中有任何点比 b 更靠近该直线，就用那个点来替换 b，我们就得到了两个新的点，然后我们取由这两者张成的新平行四边形。
But if there are any points in P closer to b, replace b by that point, and we have two new points, and we take a new parallelogram now spanned by those two things.

161
00:33:29,709 --> 00:33:38,689
我们最初由 a 和 b张成的平行四边形出发，但我们可能在内部找到了一个对于我们的目标比点 b 更好的点。
So we started with our parallelogram spanned by a and b, but we might have found a point inside that was a little bit better for our usage than the point b.

162
00:33:38,689 --> 00:33:46,952
所以现在我们用这个来替换平行四边形，此时这必定是最近的点，因为新的平行四边形包含在原先的之中。
So now we replace the parallelogram by this, where now this is certainly the closest point because this parallelogram was contained in the other one.

163
00:33:46,952 --> 00:33:53,240
这就是平行四边形中最靠近直线 a 的点。
This is the point in the parallelogram closest to this line a.

164
00:33:53,240 --> 00:34:12,520
好的。现在我断言：在这个平行四边形中，没有其他点像点 b 一样靠近直线 a，因为在平行四边形内部没有其他的点，这一点我们是确切知道的。
Okay. Now, I claim that there are no other points in this parallelogram as close to this line a as the point b, because there are no points inside the parallelogram, we certainly know that.

165
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:26,281
现在，可能有人怀疑在这条边上会有一样近的点，或者在这条边上的某处会有一样近的点。
Now, there might be a point that we thought was as close that lay on this line, or there might be a point that we thought was as close that was on somewhere on this line.

166
00:34:26,281 --> 00:34:39,495
但如果这条线上有更近的点，那么通过减去向量 a，我们就会在原来的内部找到一个比 b 更靠近该直线的点。
But if there were a point that were closer on this line, then by subtracting the vector a from it, we would have found a point that was closer to this line than b because it was here.

167
00:34:39,495 --> 00:34:52,553
所以在这条线上不可能有任何点；而这条对边上的所有点到直线 a 的距离都恰好等于 b 的距离。所以在那条线上没有更近的点。
So there can't be any points on this line, and all these points on this line are exactly as far from the line a as b is. So there are no such points on that line.

168
00:34:52,553 --> 00:34:58,640
因此我们现在知道，在平行四边形的整个闭包中，b 是离这条直线最近的点。
So now we know that in the entire closure of the parallelogram, b is the closest point to this line here.

169
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:08,280
现在的断言是：L 由 a 的整数倍与 b 的整数倍生成，L = Z a + Z b。
And now the claim is that L is generated by multiples of a and multiples of b.

170
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:20,021
因此经过这些调整后——这些调整是必要的：在直线的情形下我们做了调整，用离原点最近的向量替换了线上的向量；在此时我们最初做了调整，
So after these adjustments—and these adjustments are necessary: here we had to make an adjustment where we replaced our vector on the line by the closest vector to zero; here we initially made an adjustment that we took

171
00:35:20,021 --> 00:35:31,225
取了各条线上的最短向量，但随后我们可能还需要做一次调整，因为我们一开始可能选错了两条直线。你看，我们不想从这两条线开始，因为在这条线上还有向量。
the shortest vectors on the line, but then we still may have to have made an adjustment because we may have taken the wrong two lines to begin with. See, we wouldn't want to have started with these two lines because there were vectors on this line.

172
00:35:31,225 --> 00:35:41,986
所以我们通过在最初选取的平行四边形内取最近的向量找到了那个向量。然后断言是：所有向量都由 a 和 b 生成。
So we found that vector by taking the closest vector inside the parallelogram of our initial choice. And then the claim is that everything is spanned by a and b.

173
00:35:41,986 --> 00:36:02,200
证明如下：R^2 中的任意向量 v 都是 a 和 b 的实线性组合，对吧，其中 r 和 s 是实数，因为 a 和 b 构成一组基。
And here's the proof: any vector v in R^2 is a real combination of a and b, right, where r and s are real numbers, because a and b give a basis.

174
00:36:02,200 --> 00:36:06,254
就像那条线上的任意点都是 b 的实数倍一样。
Just like any point on this line was a real multiple of b.

175
00:36:06,254 --> 00:36:23,726
现在我把它写成整数倍 a 加上 r_0 · a，再加上整数倍 b 加上 s_0 · b：即 n · a + r_0 · a + m · b + s_0 · b，
And now I write it as an integer times a plus r_0 · a plus an integer times b plus s_0 · b, where this is an integer and this is some

176
00:36:23,726 --> 00:36:35,879
其中 n 是整数，r_0 介于 0 到 1 之间，m 是整数，且这是一个数，s_0 是介于 0 到 1 之间的某个数。
number between 0 and 1, and this is an integer, and this is some number, s_0 is some number between 0 and 1.

177
00:36:35,879 --> 00:36:47,085
如果这个向量属于 L，那么当我减去 n · a 和 m · b 时，我得到 L 中的另一个向量，因为 a 和 b属于 L。
And if this vector is in L, then if I subtract n · a and m · b, I get another vector in L, because a and b are in L.

178
00:36:47,085 --> 00:36:58,680
因此 a 的任意整数倍加上 b 的任意整数倍都在 L 中。这就意味着 r_0 a + s_0 b 属于 L。
So any multiple of a plus any multiple of b is in L. And that implies that r_0 a + s_0 b is in L.

179
00:36:58,680 --> 00:37:12,627
好的，但这正是该平行四边形中的一个向量，因为平行四边形恰好就是 a 的倍数加上 b 的倍数且倍数都小于等于1。
Okay, but this is a vector in the parallelogram, because the parallelogram is exactly the multiples of a plus the multiples of b with the multiples being less than or equal to 1.

180
00:37:12,627 --> 00:37:14,088
这里是向量 a + b。
This is the vector a + b.

181
00:37:14,088 --> 00:37:34,469
而这里的每个点都只是 a 的倍数加上 b 的倍数，其中倍数都小于等于 1。既然我们已经确定 b 是平行四边形中最靠近直线 a 的向量，那么在该平行四边形内部就不可能有其他交点。
And everything here is just some multiple of a plus some multiple of b where the multiples are less than or equal to 1. And since we've identified that b is the vector in the parallelogram closest to a, there can't be any other intersections inside that parallelogram.

182
00:37:34,469 --> 00:37:37,000
因此这个向量必须是零向量。
So this vector is zero.

183
00:37:38,520 --> 00:37:45,240
由此推知，我们原本属于该格点群的向量就是 a 的整数倍加上 b 的整数倍。
And consequently, our vector which was in the lattice was a multiple of a plus a multiple of b.

184
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:47,480
这是一个值得仔细体会的精彩论证。
So this is a good argument to go over.

185
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:56,323
我们在平面上构造了一个区域，它与 L 的交集仅仅包含其顶点。
We've constructed a region in the plane that has only its vertices as its intersection with L.

186
00:37:56,323 --> 00:38:04,570
因此 P ∩ L就只是集合 {0, a, b, a + b}。
So P ∩ L is then just the set {0, a, b, a + b}.

187
00:38:04,570 --> 00:38:19,720
因此它不可能包含任何形如这种形式且 r_0 和 s_0 都小于 1 的向量，除非 r_0 和 s_0 同时为 0；在那种情况下，该向量原本就是 a 与 b 的整数倍线性组合。
And therefore it cannot contain any vector of this form where both r_0 and s_0 are less than 1, except when both r_0 and s_0 are equal to zero, in which case the vector was originally a multiple of a and a multiple of b.

188
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:22,678
好的，我们取得了重要进展。
Okay, so we've gotten somewhere.

189
00:38:22,678 --> 00:38:38,196
我们证明了：如果我有一个刚体运动群的离散子群，并考察其中的平移变换，它要么没有任何非平凡平移；要么具有由一个固定向量及其整数倍构成的平移；要么具有由两个固定向量 a 和 b 及其所有整数倍构成的平移。
We've showed that if I have a discrete subgroup of the motion group and I look at its translations, it either has no translations, it has translations by one fixed vector and its multiples, or it has translations by two fixed vectors a and b and all of its multiples.

190
00:38:38,196 --> 00:39:01,436
因此你会有沿 a 的平移、沿 2a 的平移、沿 3a 的平移、沿 b 的平移、沿 2b 的平移、沿 a + b 的平移、沿 2a + b 的平移、沿 a + 2b 的平移等等。但即便如此，这些平移之间绝不会靠得太近。
So you'd have translation by a, you'd have translation by 2a, you'd have translation by 3a, you'd have translation by b, you'd have translation by 2b, you'd have translation by a + b, you'd have translation by 2a + b, you'd have translation by a + 2b, etc. But still, those translations do not get too close to each other.

191
00:39:01,436 --> 00:39:09,423
如果你试图在 a 和 b 的整数倍之外的任何地方再加入一个平移，你就能得到任意小的平移。
If you tried to add one more translation anywhere else other than the multiples of a and b, you'd be able to get an arbitrarily small translation.

192
00:39:09,423 --> 00:39:10,919
这就是我们所阐明的。
That's what we're saying.

193
00:39:10,919 --> 00:39:30,913
好的。现在令人惊讶的是，这看起来好像“噢，我们才刚刚解决了平移部分”——其实我们几乎快完成了！因为现在我们来考虑像Gamma-bar，即 Gamma 在 O(2) 中的像。
Okay. Now, if surprisingly this stuff which looks like, "Oh, well, we've just done the translations"—well, we're almost done, because now we consider the image Gamma-bar of Gamma in O(2).

194
00:39:30,913 --> 00:39:48,852
这里我们要用到关键引理：Gamma-bar 保持子群 L 不变。
And here's the key lemma that we're going to use here: Gamma-bar preserves the subgroup L in O(2).

195
00:39:48,852 --> 00:40:06,114
也就是说，如果我将 Gamma-bar 视作通过其作为正交变换的实现作用在二维空间上，它把这个点阵（无论属于哪种情形）映到其自身。如果格点群只是零点，那说明不了什么，因为任何群都会把零点映到其自身。
Namely, if I view Gamma-bar as acting on 2-space via its realization as orthogonal transformations, it takes this lattice or whatever it is to itself. That's not saying much if the lattice is just a zero point, because any group would take the lattice to itself.

196
00:40:06,114 --> 00:40:12,919
但如果格点群是由一个元素生成的，或者更强地，由两个元素生成的，那将给出极其强有力的结论。
But if the lattice is generated by one element, or even stronger, if the lattice is generated by two elements, that's going to be a very strong statement.

197
00:40:12,919 --> 00:40:27,639
证明如下：设 b 属于 L，即平移 t_b 是 Gamma 中的一个元素。
And here's the proof: say b is in L, i.e., translation by b is an element in Gamma.

198
00:40:27,639 --> 00:40:50,040
好的。设 gamma-bar 属于 Gamma-bar，并将其提升为 O(2) 中的一个元素 A。
Okay. Say gamma-bar is in Gamma-bar, and lift it to an element A in O(2).

199
00:40:50,040 --> 00:40:54,040
换句话说，O(2) 落在 G 内部。
So in other words, O(2) inside of G.

200
00:40:54,040 --> 00:40:58,680
所以 O(2) 这个商群，你实际上可以把它看作 G 的一个子群。
So O(2), the quotient group, you can actually think of it as a subgroup of G.

201
00:40:58,680 --> 00:41:05,639
因此在 O(2) 中存在一个元素对应于这里的 gamma-bar。
So there's an element in this O(2) that maps to this gamma-bar in Gamma.

202
00:41:05,639 --> 00:41:18,735
好的。然后实际上把它提升为一个元素——这么说不太准确——把它提升为子群 Gamma 中的一个元素 gamma。对，就这样。
All right. Then actually lift it to an element—this isn't the right way to say it—lift it to an element gamma in the subgroup Gamma. There we go.

203
00:41:18,735 --> 00:41:32,520
在 Gamma 中找到一个映到 O(2) 中该元素的元素 gamma（抱歉刚才口误），然后考虑 gamma · t_b · gamma^{-1}。
So find an element in Gamma, I'm sorry, that maps to this element in O(2), and consider gamma · t_b · gamma^{-1}.

204
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:37,120
这是该平移的一个共轭元素。因此它是另一个平移。
So that's a conjugate element of this translation. So it's another translation.

205
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:45,720
这是 Gamma 中的一个元素，因为它是 Gamma 中三个元素的乘积：这个元素、这个元素、以及这个元素的逆元。
This is an element in Gamma because it's the product of three elements in Gamma: this element, this element, and the inverse of this element.

206
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:58,119
而我们关于共轭的一般公式表明，这正好是按 gamma-bar(b) 进行的平移。
And our general formula for conjugation shows that this is translation by gamma-bar(b).

207
00:41:58,119 --> 00:42:02,851
也就是说，这是 t_{gamma-bar(b)}。
Namely, this is t of gamma-bar(b).

208
00:42:02,851 --> 00:42:10,430
所以我们刚刚证明了：如果 b 是点阵中的元素，从而该平移属于 Gamma，那么新的平移也属于 Gamma，
So we've just shown that if b is an element of the lattice, so this translation is in Gamma, then this translation is in Gamma,

209
00:42:10,430 --> 00:42:24,200
这意味着 gamma-bar(b) 属于点阵；这正是说 Gamma-bar 中的元素通过这个共轭公式保持子群 L 不变。
which implies that gamma-bar(b) is in the lattice, which is saying that the elements in Gamma-bar preserve the subgroup L via this conjugation formula.

210
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:28,119
好，这个性质极其强大。
Okay, now that is very strong.

211
00:42:28,119 --> 00:42:41,319
这极其强大，因为我马上要向大家展示这给 Gamma-bar 带来了多么严格的限制！若 L = {0}，这没有任何限制。
That's very strong because I'm now going to show you how much restriction that puts on Gamma-bar. If L is zero, it means nothing.

212
00:42:44,600 --> 00:43:00,628
那时我们知道对任意 n >= 1，Gamma-bar 可以是 C_n 或 D_{2n}，因为我们可以有任意这些有限群。
Then we know Gamma-bar is either C_n or D_{2n} for any n >= 1, because we can have any of these as finite groups.

213
00:43:00,628 --> 00:43:17,159
但假设我们处于另一个极端情形：我们处于情形 3，其中 L = Z a + Z b，且 a 和 b 线性无关。
But suppose we're in the other extreme case: we're in Case 3, where L is Z a + Z b, and a and b are independent.

214
00:43:17,159 --> 00:43:41,960
我们知道 Gamma-bar 具有这种形式，但我们能得到任意的循环群或二面体群吗？我断言：Gamma-bar 只能是 C_n 或 D_{2n}，且 n 只能等于 1、2、3、4 或 6：仅此而已！
We know that Gamma-bar has this form, but can we get any cyclic or any dihedral group? I claim Gamma-bar is equal to C_n or D_{2n} with n equal to 1, 2, 3, 4, or 6: that's it!

215
00:43:41,960 --> 00:43:54,768
因此当你的离散子群中拥有一个大的平移群时，其在正交群中的像（它是一个有限子群，因为它必须稳定该点阵子群）受到了极其严苛的限制。
So that when you get a large translation group in your discrete subgroup, the image, which is a finite subgroup of the orthogonal group because it has to stabilize this subgroup, is very restricted.

216
00:43:54,768 --> 00:44:08,613
特别是，它的阶数必须小于等于 12，因为它最大只能是 n = 6 且对应 12 阶二面体群。所以这真的非常令人惊奇。
In particular, it has order less than or equal to 12, because the biggest it could be was n = 6 and the dihedral group of order 12. So this is really quite surprising.

217
00:44:08,613 --> 00:44:17,960
无论 a 和 b 是什么，而且事实上如果我们想得到其中的某些情形，a 和 b 之间必须具备非常特殊的几何关系。
No matter what a and b are, and in fact if we're going to get any of these cases, a and b are going to have to have a very special relationship to each other.

218
00:44:17,960 --> 00:44:23,320
因此在一般情况下，我们通常只会得到 n = 1 或 2。
So in the general case we're only going to get n = 1 or 2.

219
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:28,440
好的。我现在就来向大家证明这一点。
Okay. So I'm now going to prove this to you.

220
00:44:31,941 --> 00:44:46,440
记住我们有刚体运动群 G，它包含正规子群 R^2，当我们作商群时，它同构于由旋转和反射组成的正交变换群 O(2)。
Remember we had this group G, and it contained a normal subgroup R^2, and when you made the quotient, it was isomorphic to this group O(2) of orthogonal transformations.

221
00:44:46,440 --> 00:44:57,020
因此如果我们有 G 的一个子群，我们可以考察其同态像：G 通过同态映到这个商群。
So if we have a subgroup of G, we can follow the image: G maps via homomorphism to this quotient.

222
00:44:57,020 --> 00:45:12,368
所以你可以取 Gamma 中的元素并应用该同态，从而得到该商群的一个子群。这被称为 Gamma-bar。它是如果你忽略平移部分后的 Gamma 元素，部分；即 Gamma 中元素所有可能的正交/旋转部分。
So you can take the elements in Gamma and apply the homomorphism, and then you get a subgroup of this quotient group. That's called Gamma-bar. It's the elements in Gamma if you forget their translation part.

223
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:30,520
好。说它保持子群 L 不变，意味着奇妙之处在于：这个商群仍然作用在二维空间上，并且在它对二维空间的作用下，它必须保持 Gamma 中对应于平移的向量集合不变；
Okay. So to say that it preserves the subgroup L means that the miraculous thing is that this quotient group still acts on 2-space, and in its action on 2-space it has to preserve the things in Gamma that are translations;

224
00:45:30,520 --> 00:45:41,240
这正是通过共轭公式体现的：当你用 O(2) 中的元素共轭按 b 的平移时，你得到按对应变换后的向量的平移。所以你必须亲自验算一下。
and that's via this conjugation formula, that when you conjugate a translation by b by an element in O(2), you get a translation by that. So you have to actually do that.

225
00:45:41,240 --> 00:45:45,000
就是这个。记住这一点。
That's this. Remember that.

226
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:53,603
好的，我们来算一下吧。为了让大家更踏实，我想我还有时间来证明这个结论。我先粗略演示一下。
Well, let's just do it. If it makes you feel better, I still have time, I think, to prove this thing. I'm going to wave my hands at it anyhow.

227
00:45:53,603 --> 00:46:04,716
我们来看看这个公式：设 gamma 作用在向量 v 上是 A · v，对吧？而 t_b 作用在向量 w 上是 w + b，对吧？
Let's see this formula. So gamma of a vector v is say A · v, right? And t_b of a vector w is w + b, right?

228
00:46:04,716 --> 00:46:11,800
那么 gamma^{-1} 作用在向量 v 上就是 A^{-1} · v。
And then gamma^{-1} of a vector v would be A^{-1} · v.

229
00:46:11,800 --> 00:46:21,320
好的。现在让我们计算一下，当把群中这一连串元素的乘积作用在向量 v 上时会得到什么。
Okay. Now let's calculate what we get when we apply this product of elements in the group to the vector v.

230
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:26,040
抱歉绕了一点弯路。
Sorry for this deviation.

231
00:46:26,040 --> 00:46:37,680
如果我对 v 先作用 gamma^{-1}——我想求 (gamma · t_b · gamma^{-1})(v)，它就是 gamma(t_b(A^{-1} v))，
So if I do gamma^{-1} of v—so I want gamma · t_b · gamma^{-1} of a vector v, so it's gamma · t_b of A^{-1} · v, right,

232
00:46:37,680 --> 00:46:58,040
对吧，它等于 gamma(A^{-1} v + b)，对吧，而这就是 A(A^{-1} v + b) = v + A · b。
which is gamma of A^{-1} · v + b, right, which is A(A^{-1} · v + b), which is v + A · b.

233
00:46:58,040 --> 00:47:07,684
所以该变换的作用是将一个向量平移向量 A · b，其中这是指将此正交变换应用在向量 b 上。
So that this has the property of taking a vector and translating it by the vector A · b, where this means apply this orthogonal transformation to the vector b.

234
00:47:07,684 --> 00:47:22,440
所以这就是我说的：按 b 经过正交变换后的向量进行平移；既然这种共轭变换保持 Gamma，那么我们得到的这个新平移就必须落在 Gamma 中。
So that's what I mean here: translation by this orthogonal transformation of b; and since this conjugation preserves Gamma, this new translation that we get has to be in Gamma.

235
00:47:22,440 --> 00:47:29,560
因此它落在 L 中，即 Gamma 与 R^2 的交集。
So it is in L, which is the intersection of Gamma with R^2.

236
00:47:29,560 --> 00:47:49,059
到目前为止一切顺利。现在我们来看看为什么这里的 n 会受到如此惊人的限制。嗯，我要给出一个我最喜欢的论证，它与 Artin 的方法略有不同；下次课我们会从 Artin 的论证开始。
So far so good. Now let's just see why n is so incredibly restricted here. Well, I'll give you my favorite argument, which is a little different than Artin, and next time we'll start with Artin's argument.

237
00:47:49,059 --> 00:48:22,200
假设我在 Gamma-bar 中有一个元素 A，并假设它是一个旋转。我必须证明 A 的阶数只能等于 1、2、3、4 或 6，因为你所拥有的二面体群完全由其中包含哪些旋转所决定。
Suppose I have an element A in Gamma-bar, and suppose it's a rotation. I have to show that the order of A is equal to 1, 2, 3, 4, or 6, because you can determine which dihedral group you have by which rotations you have in it.

238
00:48:22,200 --> 00:48:27,639
好，如果存在任何其他的二面体群，就会包含其他阶数的旋转。
Okay, if I had any other dihedral groups, I'd have other orders of rotations.

239
00:48:27,639 --> 00:48:49,240
好的，现在考虑 A 的特征多项式。它长成这样：我断言它是 x^2 - Tr(A) · x + 1。
Okay, now consider the characteristic polynomial of A. It looks like this: I claim x^2 - Tr(A) · x + 1.

240
00:48:49,240 --> 00:48:52,359
这是一个二维变换。
It's a two-dimensional transformation.

241
00:48:52,359 --> 00:49:13,080
如果我的旋转角是 theta，且 theta = 2pi/n，那就是我正在考察的旋转，那么该迹（如果我把复数 e^{i theta} 记作 z）就是复数 z + z-bar。
And if I have a rotation by the angle theta, and theta is equal to 2pi/n, that's the rotation that I'm looking at, then this trace, if I call this complex number z, this trace is the number z + z-bar.

242
00:49:13,080 --> 00:49:21,388
对吧？好。一般而言它就是这个形式。这是一个实数。
Right? Okay. Now, that's what it looks like in general. This is some real number.

243
00:49:21,388 --> 00:49:34,600
同时我还恰好知道——我们把它写作 x^2 - t x + 1——我还恰好知道t^2 - 4 是一个负数。
And I also happen to know—so let's write it as x^2 - t x + 1—I also happen to know that t^2 - 4 is a negative number.

244
00:49:34,600 --> 00:49:45,232
t^2 - 4 必须是负数，因为这个二次多项式的根是一对共轭复数，它们不是实数。
t^2 - 4 has to be a negative number, because the roots of this quadratic polynomial are two complex conjugate numbers; they're not real numbers.

245
00:49:45,232 --> 00:49:55,879
并且根据求根公式，如果你有一个二次方程，它的根是虚数当且仅当其判别式 b^2 - 4ac（在此时为 t^2 - 4）为负。
And so by the quadratic formula, if you have a quadratic equation, its roots will be imaginary provided its discriminant b^2 - 4ac, which in this case is t^2 - 4, is negative.

246
00:49:55,879 --> 00:50:07,680
实际上，我也可能有 1 阶旋转，所以我应该加上等号：因为我可能遇到 z = 1，或者我也可能遇到 z =-1。
Actually, I could have a rotation of order 1, so I should put this: because I could possibly have z = 1 or I could possibly have z = -1.

247
00:50:07,680 --> 00:50:12,919
那是该多项式仅有的可能实根，对应于 t = 2 或 -2 的情形。
Those are the only possible real roots of this polynomial, and that would be when t is 2 or -2.

248
00:50:12,919 --> 00:50:27,160
所以对于迹我有这个不等式。另一方面，因为 A 保持这个点阵稳定，我断言：它的迹必然是一个整数！
But I have this inequality for the trace. On the other hand, because A stabilizes this lattice, I claim that the trace is an integer.

249
00:50:37,563 --> 00:51:10,722
考虑 A 关于 R^2 的这组基的矩阵：A 关于基 {a, b} 的矩阵具有整数矩阵元，因为它保持该点阵不变。因此如果你问变换 A 对 a 做了什么，
Consider the matrix of A with respect to this basis of R^2: the matrix of A with respect to the basis {a, b} has integer entries, because it preserves this lattice. So if you ask what the transformation A does to a,

250
00:51:10,722 --> 00:51:21,773
它把 a 映为 a 的整数倍加上b 的整数倍，这就是第一列；如果你问它对 b 做了什么，它把 b 映为a 的整数倍加上 b 的整数倍。
it takes it to an integer multiple of a plus an integer multiple of b, that's the first column; and if you ask what does it do to b, it takes it to an integer multiple of a plus an integer multiple of b.

251
00:51:21,773 --> 00:51:23,487
这就是它保持该子群不变的奇妙之处！
That's this amazing thing about it preserving this subgroup.

252
00:51:23,487 --> 00:51:30,440
如果你有一个具有整数矩阵元的矩阵，它的迹必定是一个整数，对吧，因为迹是对角线元素之和。
So if you have a matrix with integer entries, its trace is an integer, right, because the trace is the sum of the diagonal entries.

253
00:51:30,440 --> 00:51:40,264
好吧，如果迹是一个整数，且 t^2 - 4 <= 0，这给 t 留下的可能取值并不多。
Okay, well, if the trace is an integer and t^2 - 4 is less than or equal to 0, that does not give too many possibilities for t.

254
00:51:40,264 --> 00:51:49,004
t 只能等于 ± 2、± 1 或 0：仅此而已！
t can be equal to ± 2, ± 1, or 0: that's it!

255
00:51:50,600 --> 00:51:56,373
± 2：对应于 1 阶和 2 阶的变换。
± 2: those are the transformations of order 1 and 2.

256
00:51:56,373 --> 00:52:03,080
± 1：对应于 3 阶和 6 阶的旋转。而 0：对应于 4 阶的旋转。就这几种！
± 1: those are the rotations of order 3 and 6. And 0: that's the rotation of order 4. That's it!

257
00:52:03,080 --> 00:52:08,048
所以大家看到，当你研究离散群时开始出现的奇妙景象。
So you see this wonderful stuff that starts to occur when you do discrete groups.

258
00:52:08,048 --> 00:52:21,879
你有两样东西：你拥有全部的算术性质：你知道某个量必须是整数，因为它保持点阵；而在另一方面，你又有某个量必须在实数意义下是有界的，因为这些特征根是复数。
You have two things: you have all the arithmetic: you know something has to be an integer because it preserves a lattice; and on the other hand you have something that has to be bounded as a real number because the roots of these things were complex.

259
00:52:21,879 --> 00:52:29,300
当你把这两点结合在一起时，你就得到了一个极小的列表：落在有界区间内的整数，因此只有有限个！
And you put those two things together, you get a very small list: an integer inside a bounded interval, so there are only finitely many!

260
00:52:29,300 --> 00:52:38,440
同样地，我们之前证明 L ∩ S 为有限集时也是完全相同的论据：结合了拓扑学与算术性质。
Likewise, the same argument was used for L ∩ S is finite: that was by topology and arithmetic.

261
00:52:38,440 --> 00:52:47,560
这就是为什么离散群在数学中成为如此吸引人的课题：它们结合了你在微积分中学的知识与在代数中学的知识，绝非单一学科。
So that's why discrete groups become such an interesting subject in mathematics: they combine what you know from calculus and what you know from algebra; it's not just one subject.

262
00:52:47,560 --> 00:52:57,560
我们用到了关于实数的这种性质：这在纯代数中是没有太多意义的——代数中没有“小于等于”——但在实数集中却存在。
We're using things about the real numbers like this: this doesn't make much sense in algebra—there is no "less than or equal to" in algebra—but there is in the real numbers.

263
00:52:57,560 --> 00:53:10,874
而这在微积分中也没有太大意义：在分析看来，整数与 2.000000001 毫无区别，但在代数中却天差地别。
And this doesn't make much sense in calculus: integers are no different from 2.000000001, but it makes sense in algebra.

264
00:53:10,874 --> 00:53:17,090
因此这表明，只要我们拥有这两个独立的生成元，这个群中的旋转就会受到极其严苛的限制。
So this shows that the rotations in this group are very seriously restricted whenever we have these two independent generators.

265
00:53:17,090 --> 00:53:19,154
下次课我将在此基础上完成分类。
And next time I'll finish up the classification based on that.

266
00:53:19,154 --> 00:53:28,840
关于阶数小于等于6 的事实，Artin 有一个基于格中最短元素的不同证明，但我想向大家展示一个数论学家的证明。
Artin has a different proof of the fact that the order is less than or equal to 6, based on the shortest element in the lattice, but I thought I'd show you a number theorist's proof.

267
00:53:28,840 --> 00:53:36,109
好的，祝大家周末愉快！周一见。
Okay, have a good weekend. See you Monday.
